meta {
  name: 12 work it out now
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/_nl/analyze
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {}
}

docs {
  Understanding your data - work it out now

  Looks at a couple of real documents for every value of every small keyword field, and writes down what the coded ones mean.

  It decodes rather than transcribes: an index whose values are already words gets a one-line briefing saying there was nothing to decode, because every keyword value is sent with each request anyway.

  You never have to call this: the first question about an index triggers it and the result is kept. Calling it at deploy time just means the first person to ask a question does not wait for it.
}
